msgid ""
"Exports the whole Excel workbook or a subset of the sheets to a PDF file. If "
"you want to print hidden sheets, you will need to list them explicitely "
"under `include`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.Book.to_pdf:8
msgid ""
"Path to the PDF file, defaults to the same name as the workbook, in the same "
"directory. For unsaved workbooks, it defaults to the current working "
"directory instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.Book.to_pdf:11
msgid ""
"Which sheets to include: provide a selection of sheets in the form of sheet "
"indices (1-based like in Excel) or sheet names. Can be an int/str for a "
"single sheet or a list of int/str for multiple sheets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.Book.to_pdf:14
msgid ""
"Which sheets to exclude: provide a selection of sheets in the form of sheet "
"indices (1-based like in Excel) or sheet names. Can be an int/str for a "
"single sheet or a list of int/str for multiple sheets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.Book.to_pdf:17
msgid ""
"This argument requires xlwings ``PRO``. Path to a PDF file on which the "
"report will be printed. This is ideal for headers and footers as well as "
"borderless printing of graphics/artwork. The PDF file either needs to have "
"only 1 page (every report page uses the same layout) or otherwise needs the "
"same amount of pages as the report (each report page is printed on the "
"respective page in the layout PDF). *New in version 0.24.3.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.Book.to_pdf:24
msgid ""
"Sheet names that start with this character/string will not be printed. *New "
"in version 0.24.4.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.Book.to_pdf:26
msgid ""
"Once created, open the PDF file with the default application. *New in "
"version 0.24.6.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.Book.to_pdf:28
